  "step1_summary": "• Chief complaint: “Crazy” headache for 3 days\n• Symptom details:\n  – Onset/duration: began ~3 days ago, gradually worsened\n  – Location: global but maximal around right eye\n  – Character: dull baseline, intermittently sharper; constant with fluctuations\n  – Severity: 8/10\n  – Associated: photophobia (light hurts), transient “shooting lights” at onset, nausea (no vomiting), difficulty concentrating\n  – Aggravating/alleviating: ibuprofen (3 tabs/day) not helpful; sleep did not help; screen brightness reduced\n  – No fever, neck stiffness, focal weakness, speech difficulty, trauma, rash\n• Past medical history: none reported; no prior migraines\n• Medications/allergies: no regular meds; no known drug allergies\n• Family history: mother and sister have frequent migraines\n• Social history: 26-y-o female; IT job with heavy computer use; lives with 3 housemates; social smoker and social alcohol use; mild work stress; wears glasses since age 5\n• Vital signs / exam: not provided (tele-visit)\n• Labs/imaging: none mentioned",
